# Findings that must not fail the build, each with a reason and a date.
#
# This file is applied only to the steps that fail the pipeline. The scans that publish
# to the Security tab do not use it, so an entry here hides nothing: it says that the
# finding is known and cannot be acted on today.
#
# An entry without exp: never expires and does not belong here. The date is what forces
# somebody to look again.
#
# Empty since 2026-08-06. The three entries that used to live here, the gRPC-Go xDS RBAC
# advisory and the two golang.org/x/text ones, were all in the Go modules statically
# linked into the official rclone binary, and all three were waiting on a release of
# rclone that carried the fixes. rclone 1.75.0 is that release: it links x/text 0.40.0
# and grpc 1.84.0-dev, and the binary now reports no findings at all, not even MEDIUM.
# The entries were deleted rather than left to expire, which is what the date was for.

# crypto/x509 in the Go 1.26.9 standard library statically linked into the official
# rclone binary. rclone 1.75.2 is the latest release and no build on Go 1.26.10 exists
# yet. The fix is a denylist of intermediate certificates no longer trusted; rclone in
# this image verifies against the Alpine ca-certificates, which apk upgrade keeps
# current, so the exposure is the narrow case the denylist exists for. Delete the entry
# once an rclone release links Go 1.26.10 or later.
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-12-15
